SYNTHETIC DEMONSTRATION MATERIAL
--------------------------------

All medical necessity criteria in this repository are synthetic demonstration
criteria, modeled on publicly available Medicare coverage determination patterns
and published payer medical coverage policies. They are representative rather
than verbatim reproductions of any current national coverage determination,
local coverage determination, or plan policy.

They are NOT Humana coverage policies, and they are not the coverage policies of
any other payer. Listed procedure codes identify supported demonstration
scenarios; they do not indicate validated production applicability.

No proprietary clinical criteria products are reproduced here. MCG and InterQual
are licensed products and are not included, paraphrased, or derived from.

All clinical records in this repository are synthetic and were authored for
evaluation. No real or de-identified patient data is used, and no protected
health information is present.

NO COVERAGE DETERMINATION
-------------------------

This software produces no coverage determination, recommendation, or aggregate
score. Its output vocabulary is evidence status only. It locates passages in a
submitted record, cites them, and reports whether the located evidence supports,
contradicts, or leaves unresolved each requirement.

A licensed physician must be involved before a Medicare Advantage plan denies
coverage, and some states require medical necessity determinations to come from
a licensed professional rather than software. Nothing produced by this prototype
is a medical necessity determination, and nothing in it should be used as one.

Reviewer time savings, nursing productivity, and clinical outcomes have not been
measured. Demonstrated technical results on synthetic cases are distinct from
all three.

